invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the incomplete Jacobian addition leaves out the step that
  multiplies s1 by z2z2, so s1 is Y1 Z2 where the formula takes
  Y1 Z2^3, and every sum whose second point has Z not 1 comes out for
  another point. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the addition to the complete
  one on multiples of G with the Z the additions before left.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&s1, &a->y, &b->z);
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&s1, &s1, &z2z2);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&s1, &a->y, &b->z);
